**Stream:** `ext` = our research of the outside world · `int` = firm-held (user-uploaded case study / CV / past bid).
**Rule:** no number, credential, outcome or best-practice assertion enters the response without a
closed row + exact locator here. One row is one atomic claim; split compound claims.
External secondary sources require a primary-source search and a reason in the locator cell when
no primary source exists.
**Status:** exactly `open`, `closed`, `closed-time-sensitive`, or `superseded`.
`closed-time-sensitive` requires `Valid as of` and `Recheck by`; it remains usable only before that
date. Do not hide future work inside text such as “closed — recheck before submission”.
**Row ids:** `BR-nnn`, cited from a response section as `BR-003` (or `log #3`). Both forms are read by
lint and by the change-impact engine; a section citing an `open` row is reported, not shipped.

